 "answer_verbatim": "There isn’t one universally “best” title company—it depends on the property, lender, fees, and how responsive the team is. **For a St. Louis-area home closing, I’d start by comparing Home Title and Investors Title**: both advertise residential title and closing services, and Investors Title has a local track record highlighted in the available results. **Excel Title** is another locally owned option to check.\n\nBefore choosing, ask each for a written estimate of title, escrow, and closing fees; confirm they can meet your closing date and work with your lender; and ask who your point of contact will be. You can generally choose the title company yourself, though your purchase contract or lender may affect the process.",
